From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Fri, 17 Oct 2026 04:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] sg2000 module: full -W radio bring-up in u-boot
 (proven live)

Upgrades the board init with the exact block proven live on the EVB
carrier by the radio debug session (wlan0 + hci0 came up with this
exact sequence):

  - RTC-domain power: 0x050250AC = 0x2 and 0x050260D0 = 0x7;
  - PWR pad group to defaults;
  - CLK32K pad -> PWR_GPIO_10 (mmio 0x030010B0 = 0x3): the 32.768 kHz
    LPO clock — without it the AIC8800D80 PMU answers SDIO register
    reads but never services the message ring;
  - SDIO1 pad group to SDIO function (determinism);
  - WL_REG_ON = XGPIOA_15: mux to GPIO, reset pulse, then HIGH — so
    the kernel's single boot-time scan of the non-removable wifi-sd
    host finds the card and S35wifi brings wlan0 + hci0 up.

Also un-deadens the SLIP UART1 mmio writes (the earlier append left
them behind an early `return 0`).

---
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c
index 93c39f4..cf34654 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2000_duomodule01_sd/u-boot/cvi_board_init.c
@@ -1,19 +1,68 @@
-// Milk-V Duo Module 01 Evaluation Board — u-boot pinmux.
 //
 // Minimal headless RNSBox config: UART0 and SD run on their reset
 // multiplexing, so the only pins that need explicit setup are the
-// internal GbE PHY LEDs (same wiring as the Milk-V Duo S reference).
+// internal GbE PHY LEDs (same wiring as the Milk-V Duo S reference)
+// plus the module WiFi/BT radio bring-up (proven live on the EVB
+// carrier; the power scheme follows the Milk-V Duo S).
 int cvi_board_init(void)
 {
 	// Internal GbE PHY LEDs
 	PINMUX_CONFIG(PWR_WAKEUP0, EPHY_LNK_LED);
 	PINMUX_CONFIG(PWR_BUTTON1, EPHY_SPD_LED);
 
-	return 0;
-
 	// UART1 (SLIP to the HaLow modem): XGPIOA[28] TX / XGPIOA[29] RX,
 	// fmux func=1 — the same encoding the Sipeed SG2002 boards use for
 	// these pads.
 	mmio_write_32(0x03001070, 0x1); // GPIOA 28 UART1 TX
 	mmio_write_32(0x03001074, 0x1); // GPIOA 29 UART1 RX
+
+	// ---- WiFi/BT radio (AIC8800D80 on the Duo Module 01 -W) ----
+	// Everything below was proven live on the EVB carrier (devmem, root):
+	// without it the radio never answers SDIO and aic8800_bsp times out
+	// ('fail to set AIC_WIFI power state to 1', /sys/bus/sdio/devices empty).
+	//
+	// 1) RTC-domain power for the radio rails (the vendor sg2000_wevb_sd
+	//    board does exactly this in set_rtc_register_for_power(); the Milk-V
+	//    Duo-S v2 SDK writes 0x7 to 0x050260D0 — value proven live).
+	// 2) The 32.768 kHz LPO clock routed out of the CLK32K pad to the
+	//    module: the AIC8800D80 PMU hangs mid-boot without LPO — the ROM
+	//    answers SDIO register reads but never services the message ring
+	//    (flow-ctrl stuck at 0, first block write times out).
+	// 3) SDIO1 pad group to SDIO function (reset default is already 0 on
+	//    this SoC; written for determinism against future pad defaults).
+	// 4) WL_REG_ON = XGPIOA_15 (pad 'SPK_EN', the wifi_pin poweron-gpio of
+	//    the board dts): mux to GPIO, drive output HIGH so the kernel's
+	//    single boot-time scan of the non-removable wifi-sd host finds the
+	//    card; S35wifi's insmod order then brings wlan0 + hci0 up.
+	mmio_write_32(0x050250AC, 0x2);            // RTC: duos-s power enable
+	mmio_write_32(0x050260D0, 0x7);            // RTC: radio power domain
+	mmio_write_32(0x03001090, 0x0);            // PWR_WAKEUP0 default
+	mmio_write_32(0x03001094, 0x0);            // PWR_WAKEUP1 default
+	mmio_write_32(0x03001098, 0x0);            // PWR_BUTTON1 default
+	mmio_write_32(0x0300109C, 0x0);            // PWR_ON default
+	mmio_write_32(0x030010B0, 0x3);            // CLK32K pad -> PWR_GPIO_10 (32k LPO out)
+	mmio_write_32(0x030010D0, 0x0);            // SDIO1 D3
+	mmio_write_32(0x030010D4, 0x0);            // SDIO1 D2
+	mmio_write_32(0x030010D8, 0x0);            // SDIO1 D1
+	mmio_write_32(0x030010DC, 0x0);            // SDIO1 D0
+	mmio_write_32(0x030010E0, 0x0);            // SDIO1 CMD
+	mmio_write_32(0x030010E4, 0x0);            // SDIO1 CLK
+	mmio_write_32(0x0300103C, 0x3);            // XGPIOA_15 pad -> GPIO mode
+	{
+		volatile unsigned int i;
+		unsigned int val;
+		val = mmio_read_32(0x03020004);        // GPIOA direction
+		val |= (1u << 15);                     // pin 15 = output
+		mmio_write_32(0x03020004, val);
+		val = mmio_read_32(0x03020000);        // GPIOA output level
+		val &= ~(1u << 15);                    // WL_REG_ON low (reset)
+		mmio_write_32(0x03020000, val);
+		for (i = 0; i < 2000000; i++) {        // ~30-60 ms reset pulse
+			__asm__ volatile ("nop");
+		}
+		val = mmio_read_32(0x03020000);
+		val |= (1u << 15);                     // WL_REG_ON high = radio on
+		mmio_write_32(0x03020000, val);
+	}
+	return 0;
 }
2.43.0

